# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Krylov space {#the-krylov-space}"
msgstr "The Krylov space {#the-krylov-space}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Krylov space $\\mathcal{K}^r$ of order $r$ is the space spanned by "
"vectors obtained by multiplying higher powers of a matrix $A$, up to $r-1$, "
"with a reference vector $\\vert v \\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Krylov space $\\mathcal{K}^r$ na may order na $r$ ay ang space na "
"natatakpan ng mga vector na nakuha sa pamamagitan ng pagmumultiplika ng mas "
"mataas na power ng matrix $A$, hanggang sa $r-1$, sa reference vector "
"$\\vert v \\rangle$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}^r = \\left\\{ \\vert v \\rangle, A \\vert v \\rangle, A^2 \\vert v \\rangle, ..., A^{r-1} \\vert v \\rangle \\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}^r = \\left\\{ \\vert v \\rangle, A \\vert v \\rangle, A^2 \\vert v \\rangle, ..., A^{r-1} \\vert v \\rangle \\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the matrix $A$ is the Hamiltonian $H$, we'll refer to the corresponding "
"space as the power Krylov space $\\mathcal{K}_P$. In the case where $A$ is "
"the time-evolution operator generated by the Hamiltonian $U=e^{-iHt}$, we'll"
" refer to the space as the unitary Krylov space $\\mathcal{K}_U$. The power "
"Krylov subspace that we use classically cannot be generated directly on a "
"quantum computer as $H$ is not a unitary operator. Instead, we can use the "
"time-evolution operator $U = e^{-iHt}$ which can be shown to give similar "
"[convergence guarantees](https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.07492) as the power "
"method. Powers of $U$ then become different time steps $U^k = "
"e^{-iH(kt)}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang matrix $A$ ay ang Hamiltonian $H$, tutukuyin natin ang kaukulang "
"space bilang power Krylov space $\\mathcal{K}_P$. Sa kaso kung saan ang $A$ "
"ay ang time-evolution operator na nabuo ng Hamiltonian $U=e^{-iHt}$, "
"tutukuyin natin ang space bilang unitary Krylov space $\\mathcal{K}_U$. Ang "
"power Krylov subspace na ginagamit natin sa classical ay hindi maaaring "
"direktang mabuo sa quantum computer dahil ang $H$ ay hindi unitary operator."
" Sa halip, maaari nating gamitin ang time-evolution operator $U = e^{-iHt}$ "
"na maaaring ipakitang nagbibigay ng katulad na [convergence "
"guarantees](https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.07492) tulad ng power method. Ang mga"
" power ng $U$ ay nagiging iba't ibang time step $U^k = e^{-iH(kt)}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}_U^r = \\left\\{ \\vert \\psi \\rangle, U \\vert \\psi \\rangle, U^2 \\vert \\psi \\rangle, ..., U^{r-1} \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}_U^r = \\left\\{ \\vert \\psi \\rangle, U \\vert \\psi \\rangle, U^2 \\vert \\psi \\rangle, ..., U^{r-1} \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"See the Appendix for a detailed derivation of how the unitary Krylov space "
"allows to represents low-energy eigenstates accurately.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tingnan ang Appendix para sa detalyadong derivation kung paano ang unitary "
"Krylov space ay nagpapahintulot na tumpak na kumatawan sa mga low-energy "
"eigenstate.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Krylov quantum diagonalization algorithm {#krylov-quantum-diagonalization-"
"algorithm}"
msgstr ""
"Krylov quantum diagonalization algorithm {#krylov-quantum-diagonalization-"
"algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given an Hamiltonian $H$ that we wish to diagonalize, first we consider the "
"corresponding unitary Krylov space $\\mathcal{K}_U$. The goal is to find a "
"compact representation of the Hamiltonian in $\\mathcal{K}_U$, which we'll "
"refer to as $\\tilde{H}$. The matrix elements of $\\tilde{H}$, the "
"projection of the Hamiltonian in the Krylov space, can be calculated by "
"calculating the following expectation values\n"
msgstr ""
"Ibinigay ang Hamiltonian $H$ na nais nating i-diagonalize, una ay "
"isasaalang-alang natin ang kaukulang unitary Krylov space $\\mathcal{K}_U$. "
"Ang layunin ay makahanap ng compact na representasyon ng Hamiltonian sa "
"$\\mathcal{K}_U$, na tutukuyin natin bilang $\\tilde{H}$. Ang mga matrix "
"element ng $\\tilde{H}$, ang projection ng Hamiltonian sa Krylov space, ay "
"maaaring kalkulahin sa pamamagitan ng pagkalkula ng sumusunod na expectation"
" value\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{H}_{mn} = \\langle \\psi_m \\vert H \\vert \\psi_n \\rangle =\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert  e^{i H t_m}   H e^{-i H t_n} \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert  e^{i H m dt}   H e^{-i H n dt} \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{H}_{mn} = \\langle \\psi_m \\vert H \\vert \\psi_n \\rangle =\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert  e^{i H t_m}   H e^{-i H t_n} \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert  e^{i H m dt}   H e^{-i H n dt} \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Where $\\vert \\psi_n \\rangle = e^{-i H t_n} \\vert \\psi \\rangle$ are the"
" vectors of the unitary Krylov space and $t_n = n dt$ are the multiples of "
"the time step $dt$ chosen. On a quantum computer, the calculation of each "
"matrix elements can be done with any algorithm which allows to obtain "
"overlap between quantum states. This tutorial focuses on the Hadamard test. "
"Given that the $\\mathcal{K}_U$ has dimension $r$, the Hamiltonian projected"
" into the subspace will have dimensions $r \\times r$. With $r$ small enough"
" (generally $r<<100$ is sufficient to obtain convergence of estimates of "
"eigenenergies) we can then easily diagonalize the projected Hamiltonian "
"$\\tilde{H}$. However, we cannot directly diagonalize $\\tilde{H}$ because "
"of the non-orthogonality of the Krylov space vectors. We'll have to measure "
"their overlaps and construct a matrix $\\tilde{S}$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung saan ang $\\vert \\psi_n \\rangle = e^{-i H t_n} \\vert \\psi \\rangle$"
" ay ang mga vector ng unitary Krylov space at ang $t_n = n dt$ ay ang mga "
"multiple ng time step $dt$ na pinili. Sa quantum computer, ang pagkalkula ng"
" bawat matrix element ay maaaring gawin sa pamamagitan ng anumang algorithm "
"na nagpapahintulot na makuha ang overlap sa pagitan ng mga quantum state. "
"Ang tutorial na ito ay nakatuon sa Hadamard test. Dahil ang $\\mathcal{K}_U$"
" ay may dimension na $r$, ang Hamiltonian na na-project sa subspace ay "
"magkakaroon ng dimension na $r \\times r$. Sa $r$ na sapat na maliit "
"(karaniwang $r<<100$ ay sapat upang makuha ang convergence ng mga estimate "
"ng eigenenergy) maaari nating madaling i-diagonalize ang projected "
"Hamiltonian $\\tilde{H}$. Gayunpaman, hindi natin maaaring direktang "
"i-diagonalize ang $\\tilde{H}$ dahil sa non-orthogonality ng mga Krylov "
"space vector. Kailangan nating sukatin ang kanilang mga overlap at bumuo ng "
"matrix $\\tilde{S}$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{S}_{mn} = \\langle \\psi_m \\vert \\psi_n \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{S}_{mn} = \\langle \\psi_m \\vert \\psi_n \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This allows us to solve the eigenvalue problem in a non-orthogonal space "
"(also called generalized eigenvalue problem)\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagpapahintulot ito sa atin na lutasin ang eigenvalue problem sa non-"
"orthogonal space (na tinatawag ding generalized eigenvalue problem)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{H} \\ \\vec{c} = E \\ \\tilde{S} \\ \\vec{c}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{H} \\ \\vec{c} = E \\ \\tilde{S} \\ \\vec{c}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One can then obtain estimates of the eigenvalues and eigenstates of $H$ by "
"looking at the ones of $\\tilde{H}$. For example, the estimate of the ground"
" state energy is obtained by taking the smallest eigenvalue $c$ and the "
"ground state from the corresponding eigenvector $\\vec{c}$. The coefficients"
" in $\\vec{c}$ determines the contribution of the different vectors that "
"span $\\mathcal{K}_U$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari kung gayon na makakuha ng mga estimate ng mga eigenvalue at "
"eigenstate ng $H$ sa pamamagitan ng pagtingin sa mga ito ng $\\tilde{H}$. "
"Halimbawa, ang estimate ng ground state energy ay nakukuha sa pamamagitan ng"
" pagkuha ng pinakamaliit na eigenvalue $c$ at ng ground state mula sa "
"kaukulang eigenvector $\\vec{c}$. Ang mga coefficient sa $\\vec{c}$ ay "
"tumutukoy sa kontribusyon ng iba't ibang vector na sumasaklaw sa "
"$\\mathcal{K}_U$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![fig1.png](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-subspace-"
"diagonalization/fc662b76-8ad7-4a6c-8c49-5f08c125aee8.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![fig1.png](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-subspace-"
"diagonalization/fc662b76-8ad7-4a6c-8c49-5f08c125aee8.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Figure shows a circuit representation of the modified Hadamard test, a "
"method that is used to compute the overlap between different quantum states."
" For each matrix element $\\tilde{H}_{i,j}$, a Hadamard test between the "
"state $\\vert \\psi_i \\rangle$, $\\vert \\psi_j \\rangle$ is carried out. "
"This is highlighted in the figure by the color scheme for the matrix "
"elements and the corresponding $\\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_i$, $\\text{Prep} \\;"
" \\psi_j$ operations. Thus, a set of Hadamard tests for all the possible "
"combinations of Krylov space vectors is required to compute all the matrix "
"elements of the projected Hamiltonian $\\tilde{H}$. The top wire in the "
"Hadamard test circuit is an ancilla qubit which is measured either in the X "
"or Y basis, its expectation value determines the value of the overlap "
"between the states. The bottom wire represents all the qubits of the system "
"Hamiltonian. The $\\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_i$ operation prepares the system "
"qubit in the state $\\vert \\psi_i \\rangle$ controlled by the state of the "
"ancilla qubit (similarly for $\\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_j$) and the operation "
"$P$ represents Pauli decomposition of the system Hamiltonian $H = \\sum_i "
"P_i$. A more detailed derivation of the operations calculated by the "
"Hadamard test is given below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapakita ng Figure ang circuit representation ng modified Hadamard test, "
"isang paraan na ginagamit upang kalkulahin ang overlap sa pagitan ng iba't "
"ibang quantum state. Para sa bawat matrix element $\\tilde{H}_{i,j}$, "
"isinasagawa ang Hadamard test sa pagitan ng state $\\vert \\psi_i \\rangle$,"
" $\\vert \\psi_j \\rangle$. Ito ay naka-highlight sa figure sa pamamagitan "
"ng color scheme para sa mga matrix element at sa kaukulang $\\text{Prep} \\;"
" \\psi_i$, $\\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_j$ operation. Kaya, kailangan ng isang "
"set ng Hadamard test para sa lahat ng posibleng kombinasyon ng mga Krylov "
"space vector upang kalkulahin ang lahat ng matrix element ng projected "
"Hamiltonian $\\tilde{H}$. Ang tuktok na wire sa Hadamard test circuit ay "
"isang ancilla qubit na sinusukat sa X o Y basis, ang expectation value nito "
"ay tumutukoy sa halaga ng overlap sa pagitan ng mga state. Ang ibabang wire "
"ay kumakatawan sa lahat ng qubit ng system Hamiltonian. Ang $\\text{Prep} "
"\\; \\psi_i$ operation ay naghahanda ng system qubit sa state $\\vert "
"\\psi_i \\rangle$ na kinokontrol ng state ng ancilla qubit (katulad para sa "
"$\\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_j$) at ang operation $P$ ay kumakatawan sa Pauli "
"decomposition ng system Hamiltonian $H = \\sum_i P_i$. Ang mas detalyadong "
"derivation ng mga operation na kinakalkula ng Hadamard test ay ibinigay sa "
"ibaba.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Define Hamiltonian {#define-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Define Hamiltonian {#define-hamiltonian}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's consider the Heisenberg Hamiltonian for $N$ qubits on a linear chain: "
"$H= \\sum_{i,j}^N X_i X_j + Y_i Y_j - J Z_i Z_j$\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang natin ang Heisenberg Hamiltonian para sa $N$ qubit sa linear "
"chain: $H= \\sum_{i,j}^N X_i X_j + Y_i Y_j - J Z_i Z_j$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set parameters for the algorithm {#set-parameters-for-the-algorithm}"
msgstr "Set parameters for the algorithm {#set-parameters-for-the-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We heuristically choose a value for the time-step `dt` (based on upper "
"bounds on the Hamiltonian norm). Ref [\\[2\\]](#references)  showed that a "
"sufficiently small timestep is $\\pi/\\vert \\vert H \\vert \\vert$, and "
"that it is preferable up to a point to underestimate this value rather than "
"overestimate, since overestimating can allow contributions from high-energy "
"states to corrupt even the optimal state in the Krylov space. On the other "
"hand, choosing $dt$ to be too small leads to worse conditioning of the "
"Krylov subspace, since the Krylov basis vectors differ less from timestep to"
" timestep.\n"
msgstr ""
"Heuristically pumipili tayo ng halaga para sa time-step `dt` (batay sa upper"
" bound sa Hamiltonian norm). Ang Ref [\\[2\\]](#references) ay nagpakita na "
"ang sapat na maliit na timestep ay $\\pi/\\vert \\vert H \\vert \\vert$, at "
"mas mainam hanggang sa isang punto na magtantiya ng mas mababang halaga "
"(underestimate) kaysa sa sobrang tantiya, dahil ang sobrang pagtantiya ay "
"maaaring magpahintulot ng mga kontribusyon mula sa high-energy state na "
"masira kahit na ang optimal state sa Krylov space. Sa kabilang banda, ang "
"pagpili ng $dt$ na masyadong maliit ay humahantong sa mas masamang "
"conditioning ng Krylov subspace, dahil ang mga Krylov basis vector ay mas "
"kaunting pagkakaiba mula sa timestep hanggang timestep.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And set other parameters of the algorithm. For the sake of this tutorial, "
"we'll limit ourselves to using a Krylov space with only five dimensions, "
"which is quite limiting.\n"
msgstr ""
"At itakda ang iba pang parameter ng algorithm. Para sa layunin ng tutorial "
"na ito, limitahan natin ang ating sarili sa paggamit ng Krylov space na may "
"limang dimension lamang, na medyo nakakahangganan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "State preparation {#state-preparation}"
msgstr "State preparation {#state-preparation}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pick a reference state $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ that has some overlap with "
"the ground state. For this Hamiltonian, We use the a state with an "
"excitation in the middle qubit $\\vert 00..010...00 \\rangle$ as our "
"reference state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pumili ng reference state $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ na may overlap sa ground "
"state. Para sa Hamiltonian na ito, ginagamit natin ang state na may "
"excitation sa gitnang qubit $\\vert 00..010...00 \\rangle$ bilang ating "
